<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-192 Phase 3 precondition (bead nexus-wbfpw.43, Sam 2026-09-29):
    nexus.chunks.last_written_at, the anchor reapable(c)'s grace window keys
    on (nexus-wbfpw.15, not part of this change).

    WHY NOT created_at. created_at is write-once, so a chunk that a re-index
    re-writes (an ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE, or the metadata-only refresh of an
    identical-text chunk) gets no fresh grace: the reaper can see it as old,
    delete it between the client's chunk write and the manifest write, and
    the manifest write then fails on fk_catalog_chunks_chunk.

    THE CONTRACT. DEFAULT now() stamps an insert. The column is refreshed to
    now() by exactly the client write paths that re-write an existing chunk:
    the content upsert and the reference-only upsert (PgVectorRepository),
    batchUpdateMetadata (the have-vector branch of upsert-chunks and the
    identical-text branch of the combined write), and the combined write's
    chunk upsert (CatalogRepository#upsertManifestChunkVectors). It is NEVER
    refreshed by maintenance or stamping UPDATEs (frecency and enrichment
    metadata stamps, collection re-homing, collection rename and move): a
    refresh from those would keep dead chunks alive forever. The rule has NO
    exception: the time a chunk last lost an owner row, which reapable(c) needs
    and which is not a client write, is recorded in its own table,
    nexus.chunk_orphaned_at (vectors-021), by triggers on the manifest, and never
    by an UPDATE of nexus.chunks (that rewrote the row into every vector index).
    created_at stays write-once. ChunksWriterLastWrittenAtScanTest lists every chunks writer in
    service/src/main and fails on one that is neither refreshing nor named
    there with a reason.

    QUARANTINE AND RETURN FROM QUARANTINE DO RESET IT. The INSERTs in
    nexus.gc_quarantine_orphans_bounded (catalog-037-1) and
    nexus.gc_restore_rereferenced_bounded (catalog-043) name created_at in an
    explicit column list and omit last_written_at, so the moved row takes
    DEFAULT now(). A chunk that enters or leaves quarantine therefore gets a
    fresh grace window. That over-refreshes, which is the safe direction: it
    can delay a reap, never cause one. Those changesets have shipped and are
    not edited; ChunkLastWrittenAtIntegrationTest pins the behaviour. (An
    earlier draft of this header said the quarantine and restore functions do
    not refresh. Their ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING branch does not, their INSERT
    does.)

    KNOWN RESIDUAL, client-initiated, does NOT refresh: StagingPromoteOps'
    content INSERT (promoteCollection) and its synthetic-stub INSERT
    (finalizeTenant) are ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING. A promote that lands a chash
    already present in the collection leaves that row's last_written_at
    alone, though a client initiated it. Its manifest rows are written later
    by finalizeTenant, so the client-write-then-manifest-write gap this
    column exists for is open here too; StagingPromoteOps names the gap in
    the "RESIDUAL, honestly named" comment above the content INSERT. This
    change does not close it. reapable(c) (nexus-wbfpw.15) has to account
    for it.

    EXISTING ROWS take the value at migration time, i.e. every chunk starts
    with a full grace window at deploy. now() is STABLE, not VOLATILE, so
    ADD COLUMN stores it as a fast default: a catalog-only change with no
    table rewrite and no long ACCESS EXCLUSIVE hold on a table this size.

    No DATA EFFECT: a bare ADD COLUMN, no row is changed or removed. No RLS
    or grant change: the tenant_isolation policy is row-scoped, and the
    nexus_svc DML grants are table-level.

    Placed after catalog-044 (the tail when this landed) and before the
    grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block (D0.1 late-append convention).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="vectors-020-1" author="nexus-wbfpw.43">
        <comment>nexus.chunks.last_written_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(): the reapable(c) grace anchor. Refreshed only by client re-writes of an existing chunk, never by maintenance or stamping updates; created_at stays write-once. Existing rows take the migration time. Fast default, no table rewrite.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks
    ADD COLUMN last_written_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now();
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            ALTER TABLE nexus.chunks DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS last_written_at;
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
